      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should comment that tracking the max bound is the best tracking because the pipeline layout packs everything at the start of the range so we can reset exactly the correct slots with a single call for the whole range.",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "311b7d97_f7063935",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BindGroupTrackerD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T10:06:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can know the max bindings used without tracking each binding (if that turns out to be unnecessary) as the pipeline layouts should know how many slots of each type are used for each stage. I also wonder if we should hardcode the D3D11 max number of bindings to use a stack variable here that would contain a bunch of zeroes, or a static variable.",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1dc9836c_9feb8ac2",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BindGroupTrackerD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T10:34:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We can know the max bindings used without tracking each binding (if that turns out to be unnecessary) as the pipeline layouts should know how many slots of each type are used for each stage\n\nThe BindGroupTracker only resets at the end of the render pass. That would go through multiple pipelines. Besides I think tracking max bindings comes naturally with the `BindingSlot` instead of adding another counting variable.\n\n\u003e I also wonder if we should hardcode the D3D11 max number of bindings to use a stack variable here that would contain a bunch of zeroes, or a static variable.\n\nThat would need to zeroize the large stack variables (default D3D11 slots can be huge such as 128 resource slots). It\u0027s not very expensive but it should be more expensive that zeroize InlinedVector with minimal 4 slots (it\u0027s common to use 4 slots or less) I think.",
      "parentUuid": "311b7d97_f7063935",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "744bdf85_681cde13",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BindGroupTrackerD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T10:06:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since we are resetting here, do we need to keep render targets? I don\u0027t know if an option is better than another perf-wise.",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5ef2e1f_9e8bfff2",
