      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T10:34:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Resetting render targets is currently done outside `BindGroupTracker`.",
      "parentUuid": "744bdf85_681cde13",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf9adfaa_a56a1f6c",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BindGroupTrackerD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T10:06:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Bindings are grouped by type in the bind group layout, so if it would help performance, we could iterate all the uniform buffers, then all the storage buffers, etc. This way the Set* function would be called at most once per bind group.",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4410f52f_7f98f98c",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BindGroupTrackerD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T10:34:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Grouping buffers in one bind call requires them to be bound to a continuous range. This is not guaranteed. Furthermore, we cannot avoid redundant bindings that way.\n\nI think it\u0027s unclear whether binding all in one D3D call even if there are redundancies is faster than binding separately but redundancies are avoided. The current code already goes with separate call model so we could fix that 1st.",
      "parentUuid": "cf9adfaa_a56a1f6c",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
