      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T10:06:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is caching a net win overall? Any perf numbers that show the effect (and separately the effect of resetting only the max used bindings on pass end?). Overall we could also just check if the bindgroup changes instead of individual resources, since we have them grouped in the WebGPU API. But also apps should avoid binding the same bindgroup redundantly, and group resources in bindgroup by change frequency.\n\nBut maybe perf numbers for Graphite show that it is necessary.",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a47c3b63_c82ba2c3",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BindGroupTrackerD3D11.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T10:19:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We already check for bind group changes in [1]. That\u0027s not enough to eliminate all redundancies because D3D11 doesn\u0027t have native BindGroup concept.\n\nIf BG1 has `{A, B, C}` and BG2 has `{D, B, C}`, there will still be redundant bindings of `{B, C}`.\n\nI saw `Commandbuffer::Execute`\u0027s time cut by half by removing the redundant bindings:\n- Before change (298ms): https://pprof.corp.google.com/?id\u003d4a8a04f7ce4a329b4931e275cdaa0f7b\u0026pivot\u003d%5Edawn::native::d3d11::CommandBuffer::Execute$\n- After change (168ms): https://pprof.corp.google.com/?id\u003dffdb3db8da6415fb1d1c004111fb544c\u0026pivot\u003d%5Edawn::native::d3d11::CommandBuffer::Execute$",
      "parentUuid": "1129ac26_3b4c6dd3",
      "revId": "95257fd5dc5b9e4be70a5dd65e0127c2d378900d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
